                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">F. T.
                            Freeman</persName>, Hampstead, sold 1902.</provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">J. &amp; J. Leighton, sold to <persName
                            role="fmo">Charles William Dyson Perrins</persName>, 1905. His MS 12.
                            Dyson Perrins was the last known owner reported in the second edition of
                            Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), with a note explaining that
                            the manuscript was sold 29 November 1960, lot 110. No update on the
                            location was provided in the Medieval Libraries of Great Britain
                            Supplement (1987).</provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">The manuscript remains untraced.
                            Compare Schoenberg Database of Manuscripts <ref
                            target="https://sdbm.library.upenn.edu/manuscripts/4372"
                            >SDBM_MS_4372</ref>, where the last known location is recorded as Sam
